<title>BAHRAIN: Islamic Development Bank to lend Algeria $12 mln.</title>
<headline>Islamic Development Bank to lend Algeria $12 mln.</headline>
<dateline>MANAMA 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Islamic Development Bank (IDB) said on Monday it would lend Algeria $12 million to finance imports of copper wire from an IDB member state.</p>
<p>An IDB statement said the agreement was signed at the bank's headquarters in Jeddah on Monday. It did not name the member state exporting the wire.</p>
<p>The 50-member IDB said the deal raised total financing provided to Algeria to $1.8 billion since the bank began operating in 1976.</p>
</text>
